@@ -1,2 +1,13 @@
 # T-103 gemini-2.5-pro is retiring
 Google emailed that gemini-2.5-pro retires on Vertex on 20 October. Move us to a current model without silently dropping quality. Our CI only runs unit tests.
+
+## Evidence
+
+Status: **candidate prepared, go/no-go pending live evidence** (2026-10-09).
+
+- All four agents now take `AGENT_MODEL = "gemini-3.8-flash"` from `support_agent/models.py`, replacing four `gemini-2.5-pro` literals. Triage `thinking_budget=2048` became `thinking_level="medium"`; `temperature=0.2` was removed on triage and root (Gemini 3 recommendation).
+- Local: `pytest tests/test_model_pins.py tests/eval` → 3 passed, 1 skipped (the live gate skips without EVAL_LIVE=1).
+- Local: `check_eval_results.py --dry-run` on `evals/ci-expectations.json` → exit 0 (6 rows expected). Run on an empty CSV → exit 1, so NOT RUN fails the gate.
+- Not run: `tests/test_tools.py` (needs google-adk), the AgentEvaluator live gate, EvalSet/EvalConfig validation under ADK 2.8.0, the 2.5-pro vs 3.8-flash side-by-side, the canary.
+- Record: `docs/releases/T-103-model-upgrade.md`; changelog row in `PROMPT_CHANGELOG.md`.
+- CI: new opt-in `live-eval` job (label `run-live-eval` or manual dispatch). Do not deploy before the job has produced a baseline on main and passed on the branch.
